Since $\tan W=\frac{\tan Z}{1+\tan Z \tan W}=1.5\left(\frac{\sqrt{10}}{4+\sqrt{10}}\right)=\frac{1.5\sqrt{10}}{4+\sqrt{10}}$, we have $\triangle WXY$ is a right triangle with legs $WZ$ and $WY$.  Using the Next formula for area, we have $$\text{[}WXYZ\text{]}=\text{[}WXY\text{]}+\text{[}WXYZ\text{]^2}=\frac{1}{2}(90)+\frac{1}{2}(49)=\boxed{\frac{137}{2}}.$$ </think> <answer> \frac{137}{2} </answer>

